      "provenance": {
        "notes": "A fussy fern: NC State rates maintenance high and sunburn and drying are the usual faults. Watering: NC State moist to wet soil, roots must not dry out; RHS water freely in growth, sparingly in winter. Light: RHS bright indirect with good ventilation; NC State partial shade to shade, loses vigour in full sun or deep shade. Humidity: both want it high (RHS: tray of moist gravel; NC State: bathrooms, terrariums), no figure. Temperature: RHS H1C (tender), no range given. Size: NC State 1 to 2 ft by 1 to 2 ft, RHS about 60 cm in the text. Toxicity is UNKNOWN: neither page mentions it and the ASPCA maidenhair fern URL returned 404; the starter list's 'non-toxic' is unverified knowledge, so nothing is stored (schema principle: no source, never safe)."
      },
